  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The temperature and the pressure of an ideal gas are changed. Assuming that the gas is in a closed container, which of the following changes will cause its volume to definitely increase?</p>\n\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Temperature</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Pressure</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"A\">\n<td><strong>A.</strong></td>\n<td>Increase</td>\n<td>Increase</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"B\">\n<td><strong>B.</strong></td>\n<td>Increase</td>\n<td>Decrease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"C\">\n<td><strong>C.</strong></td>\n<td>Decrease</td>\n<td>Increase</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"D\">\n<td><strong>D.</strong></td>\n<td>Decrease</td>\n<td>Decrease</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
